From a180bea041b53040953c2564020c79fd6b8fd86d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:54:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/52] CUDA/HIP: fuse the GATED_DELTA_NET prologue (alpha/beta
 projections, q/k l2 norm, state gather)

Per GDN layer of qwen35 this removes 8 kernel launches:
- the alpha/beta projections and their add/softplus/mul/sigmoid tails run
  as one MMVQ launch on the cached q8_1 activations (idea from upstream
  PR #29187, here for every MMVQ quant type and up to 8 tokens);
- the GDN kernel l2-normalizes q and k itself from the RMS_NORM inputs
  (same per-element arithmetic as rms_norm + scale), so the two
  RMS_NORM(+SCALE) launches are elided;
- the GDN kernel reads its initial state through the s_copy index from the
  recurrent cache, so the GET_ROWS gather of the state is elided
  (single sequence only; each thread reads its state before writing
  its snapshots, so slot rows may alias the source row).
Elided nodes are skipped by ggml_cuda_try_fuse returning -1; the GDN-side
predicates are used for both the skip decision and the kernel, so an
unelided prologue still gives the same result.
